# CKD Prediction Web App

## 1. Project Overview

The CKD Prediction Web App is a Machine Learning-based web application developed to assist in the prediction of Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) based on selected clinical parameters.

The application provides a web-based interface where users can enter patient information and obtain a prediction from a trained Machine Learning model. It also provides patient record management and PDF report generation.

This project demonstrates the integration of Machine Learning, Python, Flask, SQL database management, and frontend web technologies into a single application.

---

## 2. Problem Statement

Chronic Kidney Disease is a condition that can develop gradually and may not show obvious symptoms during its early stages. Analysing multiple clinical parameters can be useful for identifying patterns associated with CKD.

The objective of this project is to develop a web application that uses a trained Machine Learning model to predict CKD based on patient clinical data.

---

## 3. Project Objectives

The main objectives of the project are:

- To develop a Machine Learning model for CKD prediction.
- To create a user-friendly web interface for entering patient information.
- To integrate the trained model with a Flask web application.
- To store patient information and prediction records in a database.
- To provide prediction results through the web application.
- To generate downloadable PDF reports.
- To organize the project using a maintainable application structure.

---

## 4. Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python | Application and Machine Learning development |
| Flask | Web application framework |
| Flask-SQLAlchemy | Database integration |
| Flask-Migrate | Database migrations |
| Flask-Mail | Email functionality |
| Pandas | Data processing |
| Scikit-learn | Machine Learning |
| Joblib | Model saving and loading |
| HTML | Web page structure |
| CSS | Web page styling |
| JavaScript | Frontend functionality |
| SQLite | Database |

